-## 6. Mode isolation and fallback
-
-Apply routing per output. Before the first human progress message, read the installed `caveman/SKILL.md` for its style rules; before the first agent-facing natural-language output, read `ultracave/SKILL.md`. Use the verified skill-file location for the current host (normally `~/.agents/skills/<name>/SKILL.md`). Read once per session unless the file changes or its content is incomplete in context. **Reading is not invoking**: treat session-wide persistence and mode-switch instructions as inactive unless the user explicitly invokes that mode. Do not activate or switch a persistent session-wide Caveman mode merely to format a single progress message, agent message, or artifact. Names in a policy do not themselves prove automatic loading. Respect any explicitly selected mode or output contract that has higher applicable priority.
